   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing Christopher Walser to take the competitive\ncivil service examination for the position of police officer and be placed on\nthe eligible list for employment as a full-time police officer for the village\nof Skaneateles police department",
    "basePrintNo": "S1232",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1232-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1232\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing Christopher Walser to take the compet-\nitive civil service examination for the position of police officer and\nbe placed on the eligible list for employment as a full-time police\nofficer for the village of Skaneateles police department\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would allow for Christopher Walser to complete the\ncivil service examination for the position of police officer, despite\nthe age requirement.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Allow for Christopher Walser to be eligible under civil\nservice law, including the age requirement under paragraph (a) of subdi-\nvision 1, for the civil service examination for the position of police\nofficer. Should Christopher Walser score accordingly, he will be placed\non the eligible list for appointment as a police officer with the\nvillage of Skaneateles police department.\n\nSection 2. Christopher Walser will be subject to the merit and fitness\nprovisions of the civil service law applicable to full-time police offi-\ncers.\n\nSection 3. Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChristopher Walser served as a police officer in North Carolina before\nmoving to New York State. However, his certifications did not transfer\nacross state lines, and he would like the opportunity to serve the resi-\ndents of the village of Skaneateles by continuing his work as a police\nofficer.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-2024 - S.3512-A (May) / A.3900-A (Lemondes)\n\n2021-2022 - S.8329 (Mannion) / A.10340 (Lemondes)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
