   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing Christopher Walser and Matthew Patire to\neach take the competitive civil service examination for the position of police\nofficer and be placed on the eligible list for employment as a full-time\npolice officer for the village of Skaneateles police department",
    "basePrintNo": "S1232",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1232-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1232A\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing Christopher Walser and Matthew Patire\nto each take the competitive civil service examination for the position\nof police officer and be placed on the eligible list for employment as a\nfull-time police officer for the village of Skaneateles police depart-\nment\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would allow for Christopher Walser and Matthew Patire\nto complete the civil service examination for the position of police\nofficer, despite the age requirement.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Allow for Christopher Walser and Matthew Patire to be eligi-\nble under civil service law, including the age requirement under para-\ngraph (a) of subdivision 1, for the civil service examination for the\nposition of police officer. Should Christopher Walser and Matthew Patire\nscore accordingly, they will be placed on the eligible list for appoint-\nment as a police officer with the village of Skaneateles police depart-\nment.\n\nSection 2. Christopher Walser and Matthew Patire will be subject to the\nmerit and fitness provisions of the civil service law applicable to\nfull-time police officers.\n\nSection 3. Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChristopher Walser and Matthew Patire would like the opportunity to\nserve the residents of the village of Skaneateles by continuing his work\nas a police officer. However, they have aged out of the Civil Service\nExam. This bill was introduced at the request of the Skaneateles Police\nDepartment.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-2024 - S.3512-A (May) / A.3900-A (Lemondes)\n\n2021-2022 - S.8329 (Mannion) /A.10340 (Lemondes)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
